# Keep Jig source-linked from `.dependencies/jig/source`

Keep Jig source-linked from `.dependencies/jig/source`.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Keep Jig source-linked from `.dependencies/jig/source`.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

The local development installation resolves `.dependencies/jig/source` to the
sibling Jig checkout. Tracked `.jig/jig.toml` routes CSpell, Git, Markdownlint,
nightly Cargo/Clippy/rustfmt, and stable Cargo through that source-linked
boundary. A repository architecture test parses the tracked TOML and fails if
those shared tool paths bypass `.dependencies/jig/source/`.

`docs/technical/validation/deterministic-validation.md` now documents which Jig
state is tracked versus ignored/local and keeps source code out of SHAR. The
source link itself remains machine-local dependency state rather than a tracked
repository symlink.
